      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-47476",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/52/52ca3977b5b6a1fe636c664743e02e135c6dcda788ea329aace4841f9436b1b6.png)\n\nA blimp is flying over a soccer stadium. At a particular moment, the blimp is $720yards$ from the northern end zone and $570yards$ from the southern end zone. Find the angle of elevation from the northern end zone to the blimp if the elevation angle from the southern end zone to the blimp is $51^{\u2218}$. Round the answer to two decimal places.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
