      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-47479",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/fd/fd0a968d33ecdd74f5447e66c95be3da0b9a05a14938e40381aba55beb0c85f1.png)\n\nLena, Jerry, and Matilda set three separate huts in a forest. Lena and Jerry's huts are $10.3m$ apart, while Jerry and Matilda's huts are $6.1m$ apart. From Matilda's point of view, the angle between Lena's and Jerry's huts is $23^{\u2218}$. What is the angle between Jerry's and Matilda's huts from the point of view of Lena? Round the answer to one decimal place.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
